WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.580
Yo' what it is?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.020
Sparky Sweets again.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:17.440
And this week we reppin' down South with 
To Kill A Mockingbird by Harper Lee.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.280
This book focuses on three little homies
by the name of Scout,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.520
her crippled brother Jem,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.320
and some homeboy by the name of Dill.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.680
Now, Scout's papa is a righteous lawyer
with the badass name of Atticus.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.080
Since there ain't nothing to do in Alabama,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.560
Scout and her crew spend a summer 
harassing a nearby shut-in named Boo Radley.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.320
Now, ain't nobody seen Boo Radley for years.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.280
Scout and her crew try to pass Boo
a note to see if he wants to chill,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.520
but Atticus gets all crunk 
and tell dem' kids to "Leave a brother be."

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.800
Next day, some little punk steps to Scout...

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.920
...and straight up calls Scout's daddy, Atticus, a "Nigger lover."

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:56.720
Mmmm!

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.840
Turns out, Atticus has been hired to defend 
some ashy playa' named Tom Robinson,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.280
who has been accused of raping 
the daughter of a shady cat named Bob Ewell.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.360
At the trial, my boy Atticus spits 
mad game up in that court room.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.960
In fact, he discover it was Ewell's daughter
that was puttin' the moves on Tom.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.760
Turns out she wanted some of that
"dark chocolate," know what I mean?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.600
After seeing his daughter 
makin' advances on a brotha,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.440
Mr. Ewell smack that bitch up raw, 
while Tom peaced out.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.280
But since we talkin' about Alabama here, 
them white folks convict him anyway.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.280
Why?

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.262
Cuz' he black.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.520
That honky Ewell be pissed that Atticus
made him look like a fool up in court,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.280
so Halloween night, Ewell downs too much of
that juice and gets the drop on Jem and Scout.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.800
Just when he about to rough up my girl, Scout, crazy cracka' Boo Radley comes in outta nowhere,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.680
and shanks that fool. Whoo!

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.960
He dead.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.320
Sick and tired of his stupid lip,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.600
the town authorities decide that Ewell 
got too drunk and fell on his knife.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.719
Boo gets off Scott free.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.503
Why?

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:06.120
Cuz' icing him, like my girl Scout says, 
would be like "Shootin' a mockingbird."

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.920
Now, you all don't know sh*t about the title
until you read this here quote on page 90:

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.160
Only a jive-ass fool would 
pop a cap in a mockingbird,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.800
cuz' all dem bitches do is just drop 
next level beats for your enjoyment.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.280
So what my girl, Harper, tryin' to say is that 
rattin' on Boo Radley wouldn't do no good.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.560
It only rid the hood of one more true blue playa.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.120
They already done f*cked up once by convictin' Tom,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.960
so they ain't got to pop another mockin' bird.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.080
Now this book right here is a straight up
criticism of the South during The Depression.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.200
The courts, the schools, the church: 
all of 'em were run by crooked ass crackas.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.320
Now when we first meet Scout, she's sportin' 
all that Southern racism and ignorance.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:59.280
But after kickin' it with Boo and Tom Rob, 
she matures and starts keepin' it real.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.000
Dis' brings to one of the essential 
themes of this bitch:

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.560
learning valuable lessons by being 
exposed to people of difference.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.640
By hangin' with a crazy cracka' like Boo Radley 
and a righteous black man like T. Robinson,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:15.320
Scout has one of them 
paradigm shiftin' moments, playa.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:19.320
She learns that these homies
just be tryin' to hustle like anybody else.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.040
Yo! Check it.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.480
Jim's crippled ass is a metaphor 
for America's jacked up justice system.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.400
Jim f*ckin' up his arm so young 
be one of them synecdoches

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.600
for a country that was born with backward ass ideals.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.080
Now, that sh*t might heal, but it gonna leave
a disabling scar on the nation

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:40.040
and ain't no amount of cocoa butter 
gonna make that sh*t go away.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.280
Yo! Thanks for watchin' Thug Notes.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.249
Tune in next week, playa.

